course: dictionary
lesson: 15380
title: Specialisation: becoming an expert
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Specialisation means focusing on one subject, skill or job and becoming an expert in it. Look at the clues here: «Dr Patel chose a specialisation, so she is a heart doctor and only treats hearts.» Only treats hearts tells you that a specialisation is one special area of work.
explain: The word can also name the subject or area itself. «Her specialisation is maths, and she loves solving tricky puzzles.» Her specialisation is what she focuses on, so here it means the area she is an expert in. Try your meaning in the sentence to check it.
explain: In science, specialisation describes cells and body parts. «Red blood cells have a special shape to carry oxygen around the body.» Each cell is shaped for one job, so this is cell specialisation. Does "a special shape for one job" fit the sentence? Yes, so you have it.
fact: Specialisation means focusing on one subject, skill or job and becoming an expert in it.
fact: Specialisation can also mean the particular subject or area that someone focuses on, like «her specialisation is maths».
fact: In science, cell specialisation means a cell has a special shape for its one job, like red blood cells or nerve cells.
fact: In history and economics, specialisation means people doing one job well and trading with each other.
fact: Specialisation is a noun, and you can have one specialisation or several specialisations.
exercise: «Dr Patel's specialisation is hearts, so she only treats patients with heart problems.» What does specialisation mean here? | Going on holiday to the seaside | Doing lots of different jobs at once | *Focusing on one special area and becoming an expert in it | A type of very loud music
exercise: Red blood cells, nerve cells and muscle cells each have a special shape for their job. What is this called? | *Cell specialisation | Cell holidays | Cell fishing | Cell weather
exercise: «Farmers grow wheat, bakers make bread, and they trade with each other.» Which word describes each person doing one job well? | *Specialisation | Hibernation | Decoration | Celebration
test: «Mo has a specialisation in drawing horses.» What does specialisation mean here? | The number of hours Mo sleeps each night | A large, bouncy ball | *The area Mo focuses on and is an expert in
test: Nerve cells are long and thin so they can send messages fast. What is this an example of? | *Cell specialisation | Cell shopping | Cell sleeping
exam: Lily says, «I want a specialisation, not a little bit of everything.» What does Lily mean? | She does not like maths | She wants to do lots of jobs badly | She wants to stop learning | *She wants to become an expert in one area
